cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Field in research or teaching, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Field: an offline-first fitness testing and performance tracking app for coaches"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gunda
    given-names: Vamshi
    affiliation: Azim Premji University
version: 1.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23208441
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vamshigunda-star/Field"
abstract: >-
  Field is an offline-first Android app for coaches, PE teachers and fitness
  professionals. It runs fitness testing events for athlete groups, records
  results on the spot (including a built-in stopwatch for timed tests), and
  classifies each result against age- and sex-bracketed percentile norms
  derived from published exercise-testing standards, so performance can be
  tracked over time without a network connection.
keywords:
  - fitness testing
  - physical education
  - sports science
  - performance assessment
  - normative data
  - coaching
  - Android
  - offline-first
